the target language is: prolog.

the functions are:
    the tax delinquent of the simple checks of the situation is *a truth value*.
    the property tax payment plan of the simple checks of the situation is *a truth value*.
    the check result is *a truth value*.
    the tax delinquent service result is *a truth value*.

the knowledge base property_taxes_current_or_payment_plan includes:

the text of the_model is at "sources/property-taxes-current-or-payment-plan.dmn".

rule tax_delinquent_service_1 with provenance the model at decision TaxDelinquentService:
the tax delinquent service result is true if
    the tax delinquent of the simple checks of the situation is true.

rule tax_delinquent_service_2 with provenance the model at decision TaxDelinquentService:
the tax delinquent service result is false if
    the tax delinquent of the simple checks of the situation is false.

rule check_result_1 with provenance the model at decision checkResult:
the check result is true if
    the tax delinquent service result is false.

rule check_result_2 with provenance the model at decision checkResult:
the check result is true if
    the property tax payment plan of the simple checks of the situation is true.

rule check_result_3 with provenance the model at decision checkResult:
the check result is false if
    the tax delinquent service result is true
    and the property tax payment plan of the simple checks of the situation is false.

scenario Delinquent_with_unknown_plan is, as stated in the Bruno requests of PropertyTaxesCurrentOrPaymentPlan at test case Delinquent with unknown plan:
    the tax delinquent of the simple checks of the situation is true.
